[SO-4956709] Q: Browser compatibility of some type of css selectors
A: <p>IE7 and newer, as well as all other browsers, support all your given selectors.</p>

<ol>
<li><p>IE6 reads <code>.class-1.class-2</code> as <code>.class-2</code> (see <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/3772290/css-selector-that-applies-to-elements-with-two-classes/3772305#3772305">here</a> for a comparison)</p></li>
<li><p>IE6 parses <code>#id-1.class-2</code> correctly</p></li>
<li><p>IE6 cannot read <code>&gt;</code>, ignores entire rule completely</p></li>
<li><p>IE6 cannot read <code>+</code>, ignores entire rule completely</p></li>
<li><p>IE6 cannot read <code>[foo="bar"]</code>, ignores entire rule completely</p></li>
</ol>


