[SO-32440276] Q: QuickFix multileg order rejected on tag 167 set to MLEG at Interactive Brokers
A: <p>MsgType AB (NewOrderMultileg) was only added in FIX 4.3, so I suspect this is the cause of the “Unsupported type” message.  You’ll notice you were getting this error in your first example too, where your tag 167 value was being rejected.</p>

<p>Adding the new value to your dictionary is the correct way to add it as a valid value your end.</p>

<p>I suspect your broker actually expects you to send a NewOrderSingle message (35=D) with the MLEG value and any other custom fields, to replicate the functionality of the NewOrderMultileg.  Failing that, you'd need to use a more up-to-date version of the FIX protocol (probably 4.4 or 5.0)</p>

<p>Cheers,
Campbell</p>


